# Copy to .env at your library root (the directory you start the server from)
# and fill in values as needed. Loaded automatically on server start; a missing
# .env is fine -- nothing here is required. Real environment variables win.

# The library root is NOT configured here -- it is the working directory the
# server is launched from, and the catalog is always <library root>\.catalog.

# search_rpg_geek / lookup_rpg_geek_product call the RPGGeek XML API.
# Optional -- basic search/lookup works unauthenticated; set this to raise
# RPGGeek's rate limits if you have a bearer token.
# RPGGEEK_BEARER_TOKEN=...

# search_dtrpg calls the DriveThruRPG vBeta API. Required for that tool to
# work at all -- an application key from your DriveThruRPG account.
# DTRPG_API_KEY=...

# lookup_isbn falls back Google Books -> Open Library -> Wikidata. Optional
# -- Open Library/Wikidata work without it; setting this adds Google Books
# (higher quota, and the only one of the three that returns a description).
# GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=...

# read_pdfs calls an LLM (via litellm) to summarize a PDF's description and
# guess its RPG system. The model itself is checked into the repo
# (resources/llm_settings.yaml) -- set here only the credential your chosen
# model's provider needs, e.g.:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Dev use only: overrides the target database for `alembic` CLI commands
# (see README.md's "Development" section). Not read by the server itself.
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////absolute/path/to/.catalog/catalog.db
